{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SCOPE AMENDED — bug 5f48 [rebar:5f48-244c-7063-42d0] is FOLDED INTO THIS STORY by operator decision.\n\nWHY IT BELONGS HERE RATHER THAN AS FOLLOW-UP: this story's own change activates the defect. Until the\nreconciler.backend widening lands, _as_choice(v, k, {'jira'}) meant config could NEVER select the DC\nbackend, so select_backend(load_config()).vendor could never return 'jira-datacenter' and the broken\npath was unreachable. Landing the widening without the fix ships a silently-degraded DC inbound path.\n\nTHE DEFECT, measured rather than reasoned about:\n  CREATION_CHANNELS = {'cli','mcp','python','jira','import','unknown'}   # no 'jira-datacenter'\n  apply_inbound_records.py: vendor = select_backend(load_config()).vendor\n                            ensure_identity_for(vendor, ..., creation_channel=vendor)\nOn a scratch repo:\n  creation_channel='jira'            ext=acct-cloud -> returned '4802-2404-6de4-4167'\n  creation_channel='jira-datacenter' ext=acct-dc    -> ValueError: invalid creation_channel\n    'jira-datacenter'; must be one of ['cli','import','jira','mcp','python']\n\nIt only reproduces on a FRESH mint — an existing (provider, external_id) mapping is reused idempotently\nand never reaches validation. My first probe reused an identity and showed a FALSE PASS; distinct\nexternal_ids exposed it.\n\nWHY IT IS SILENT, which is what makes it dangerous: the call is wrapped in\n'except Exception:  # best-effort ghost mint; never fail the inbound apply' and logged at DEBUG. So\nevery inbound DC ghost-identity mint fails, is swallowed, and the pass still converges. That is exactly\nepic AC6's premise — a swallowed exception can still converge, so convergence is not evidence.\n\nFIX DIRECTION, and the one explicitly rejected: map the backend vendor to its FAMILY channel so Cloud\nand DC both mint under the shared 'jira' provider/channel. The ticket-creation path a few lines below\nALREADY hard-codes validate_creation_channel('jira'), so the two paths in the same module are currently\ninconsistent and the identity path is the wrong one. Widening CREATION_CHANNELS is REJECTED: it forks\nthe store vocabulary per deployment, contradicts the epic's shared-identity decision, fragments one\nhuman's identity across deployments, and pulls in the migration + compatibility gate this epic avoids.\n\nFour ACs added. Plan attestation is invalidated by this edit, so review-plan is being re-run.\n\nSEPARATELY, and NOT resolved: AC8 requires asserting 'a populated RemoteRef.instance'. RemoteRef is\nNEVER CONSTRUCTED IN PRODUCTION CODE — grep across src/ finds only the frozen dataclass definition and\ndocstrings; the sole constructions in the whole repo are in tests (backend_support.py:174 and the\nvalue-equality contract test). So no reconcile pass can populate it and that half of AC8 is not\nsatisfiable as written. Flagging rather than quietly asserting the half that works."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785469938377890001,"uuid":"0de2c54c-59ca-4c84-a13e-eb8960e2593e"}